# Security and challenges

This repository exists so SDI's claims can be checked by anyone. If a
check fails, that is exactly what this address is for:

**support@sdi-protocol.org**

Report anything in these categories:

- A hash that does not recompute: entry_hash, cognitive_hash, or parent
  linkage failing on any public chain entry.
- A metric that does not match: any MATCH/MISMATCH instrument producing
  MISMATCH on a committed act.
- An endpoint behaving differently than documented, here or on
  [sdi-protocol.org](https://www.sdi-protocol.org).
- A discrepancy between these scripts and the formulas published on the
  [verify page](https://www.sdi-protocol.org/verify).
- Anything that looks like a security issue in the public API surface.

There is no bug bounty and no disclosure embargo requested. Reports are
read by the maintainer. A failed check is the most useful mail this
project can receive, and challenges that hold will be acknowledged
plainly rather than quietly patched.
